. * =====================================================================
. * 1. The failure-mode vocabulary
. *    A suite is classified by the class of failure each test rules out.
. * =====================================================================
. stataqa families

Test families
------------------------------------------------------------------------
CODE     MEANING
------------------------------------------------------------------------
ENV      Environment and setup: dependencies present, version stamps, adopath, install integrity
SMOKE    Smoke tests: the package loads and its principal command runs at all
DET      Deterministic / offline: frozen inputs, pinned values, no network
REGR     Regression baselines: current output still matches a stored baseline
ERR      Error conditions: invalid input is rejected with the right return code
EDGE     Edge cases: N=1, empty results, special characters, boundary values
EXT      Extreme inputs: large or stress-scale queries and datasets
PERF     Performance: timing or resource assertions against a stated threshold
DATA     Data structure: variable types, value ranges, duplicates, identifiers
TRANS    Transformations: reshape, rename, derived variables, wide/long
META     Metadata operations: labels, notes, enrichment, codelist health
DISC     Discovery: search, listing, catalog queries
SYNC     Metadata synchronization: regenerating metadata from an authority
INT      Integration: interaction with a sibling package or external service
DOC      Documentation as tests: help-file examples execute
XPLAT    Cross-platform: outputs agree across languages or implementations
------------------------------------------------------------------------
A test id is FAMILY-NN, as in DET-01.  See stqa_families.

. 
